# Update the UI

**Prerequisites:** [first standalone app](/docs/tutorials/first-app/).
**You will do:** pick the handler kind that matches the intended browser result.
**Verify:** counter increment patches `#counter`; a `@command` returns empty SSE to Datastar.
**Next:** [Handle requests and errors](/docs/how-to/handle-requests-and-errors/) or
[Runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/).

`@on` is **removed**. Write `@view`, `@patch`, `@command`, or `@live`.

## Choose a shape

| Goal | Declaration | Browser result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Replace HTML in the acting tab | `@patch("path")` | One-shot `datastar-patch-elements` |
| Return data, no morph | `@command("path")` | **empty SSE** to Datastar; JSON to other clients |
| Shared HTML for every open tab | `@live` | Generated `GET /sse` |

Default mutation method is POST. Spell `:put`, `:patch`, or `:delete` when the
verb must differ. `@patch:post` is rejected. GET is rejected on `@patch` and
`@command`.

Canonical one-shot: [Counter](/examples/counter/).
Canonical stream: [Live counter](/examples/live-counter/).
Complete matrix: [Handler matrix](/examples/handler-matrix/).

## Wire the button

```rocci
<button data-on:click=@post("/actions/inc")>Inc</button>
```

`@post("/path")` is a Rocci action (Roc string, double quotes). A second
argument is a list of Datastar options. Quoted `"@post('…')"` is opaque
Datastar JS, not a Rocci action.

For row-specific URLs, make the attribute a Roc expression. A static quoted
string does not interpolate a `@for` binder.

Do not morph the same `id` from both a `@command` and `@live`. Do not bind a
visible count to `$count` to “reuse” JSON; HTML is the document, JSON is data.

**Related:** [Datastar as transport](/docs/concepts/datastar-as-transport/),
[One-shot versus live](/docs/concepts/one-shot-versus-live/).
